  "idea": "Founder async weekly standup system that eliminates hour-long syncs",
  "text": "Stop holding live meetings that could have been a structured two-minute text update. Founders fill company calendars with recurring check-ins just to verify that sprint tasks are moving forward. These interruptions fragment developer focus, turning two-hour coding tasks into week-long slogs. Connect Linear webhooks to a dedicated Slack feed that automatically surfaces task completions and review requests. This eliminates status meetings entirely while speeding up releases.",
